course: dictionary
lesson: 7693
title: Prove: show that it is true
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Prove is a verb with several meanings. The most common one is to show with facts or reasons that something is true. «Two things happening together does not prove that one causes the other.» Here prove means show clearly that it is true, and the clue is the word not: happening at the same time is not enough.
explain: Prove can also mean to turn out to be. «The test proved easy» means the test was easy once people tried it. Prove yourself means to show what you can do, as in «She proved herself a good captain.» The words around prove tell you which meaning you need.
explain: In baking, prove means to let dough rise before it is cooked. Ask yourself: is this sentence about facts, a test, or bread? Then put your meaning into the sentence in place of prove and check that it still makes sense.
explain: In science, experiments give evidence that supports or does not support an idea. In maths, you prove something by showing clear steps why it is always true. «In 1822 a stork in Germany was found with an African spear in its neck; it helped prove storks spend winter in Africa.» One clue can help, but a good proof needs strong evidence.
fact: Prove means to show with facts or reasons that something is true.
fact: «Prove» can also mean to turn out to be, as in «The test proved easy.»
fact: «Prove yourself» means to show what you can do, as in «She proved herself a good captain.»
fact: In baking, to prove dough means to let it rise before cooking.
fact: «Prove wrong» means to show that something is mistaken, as in «What would prove it wrong?»
exercise: «Two things happening together does not prove that one causes the other.» What does prove mean here? | Turn out to be easy | Let dough rise before cooking | *Show with facts or reasons that something is true | Show what you can do
exercise: «The test proved easy.» What does proved mean here? | *Turned out to be | Showed off | Lost | Cooked slowly
exercise: «She proved herself a good captain.» What is she showing? | Losing her hat | That she is hungry | *What she can do, as a good captain | Dough rising in a bowl
test: Mum says, «Leave the dough to prove for an hour before you bake it.» What does prove mean? | Show it is true | *Let the dough rise | Turn out to be easy | Prove yourself
test: «What would prove it wrong?» asks what could show an idea is mistaken. What does prove wrong mean? | Forget it | Make it bigger | *Show that it is mistaken | Make it wrong on purpose
exam: «The stork's spear helped prove storks spend winter in Africa.» Which meaning of prove is used? | *Show with facts that something is true | Show what you can do | Turn out to be easy | Let dough rise before cooking
